course: dictionary
lesson: 15311
title: Slowness: the quality of being slow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Slowness is a noun. It is the name for the quality of being slow, so we can talk about it as a thing. «The slowness of the queue made everyone sigh.» The queue moved without much speed, and the children felt it.
explain: Look at the ending. Slow plus -ness makes slowness, just as kind plus -ness makes kindness. The -ness ending turns a describing word into a naming word.
explain: Slowness has two meanings. It can mean moving, happening or working without much speed, or being slow to understand or react. «Her brother's slowness to understand the rules made the game funny.» Here the slowness is in thinking, not in moving.
fact: Slowness is a noun, so it names a quality, such as the slowness of a snail.
fact: The ending -ness changes slow into slowness, just as kind becomes kindness.
fact: «The slowness of» is often followed by a process, such as the slowness of growth or the slowness of erosion.
fact: Erosion, when wind and water wear away rock, happens so slowly that we rarely notice it.
fact: In a story, a character's slowness can be funny or worrying, depending on what happens next.
exercise: «The slowness of the queue made everyone sigh.» What does slowness mean here? | Being very happy | Standing still in the rain | Being very loud | *Moving without much speed
exercise: Which word is the noun form of slow? | slows | slowed | slowly | *slowness
exercise: «Her brother's slowness to understand the rules made the game funny.» What does slowness mean in this sentence? | Being tired of school | *Being slow to understand | Being loud and cheerful | Being very fast at maths
test: «Frustrated by the slowness of the bus, Sara walked home.» What feeling does frustrated show? | *Annoyed | Sleepy | Delighted | Proud
test: Which word ends with the same -ness ending as slowness? | *kindness | kinder | kindly | kind
exam: «The slowness of erosion means cliffs change over thousands of years.» What does this sentence tell us? | Cliffs change only when people build on them | Erosion is a kind of plant that grows on cliffs | Erosion happens very quickly, in a single day | *Erosion happens so slowly that we rarely notice it
